  ],
  "review_questions": [
    "Does the output contain the requested subject or declared class?",
    "Does it preserve the supplied source content where the task requires preservation?",
    "Which visible defects affect composition, detail, text, or color?",
    "For video, describe motion, discontinuities, flicker, and consistency across the complete clip."
  ],
  "rules": [
    "Retained input and output identities define review cases, not matched performance baselines; their generation records lack source and environment bindings.",
    "Use the inventory's pinned references and the owning component's existing numerical criteria; preserve their original requests and distinguish partial oracles from complete comparisons.",
    "Record pre-quantization finiteness from the executing numerical owner; decoded byte images alone cannot establish it.",
    "Review images at original resolution and videos across their complete frame sequence. Report each question and the reviewed artifact identity; do not turn a decode or timing result into a quality judgment.",
    "Treat Un-0 video as independent class-conditioned image generations using successive seeds; describe temporal limitations explicitly.",
    "Use the declared model/runtime frame rate: Wan and LiveEdit profiles declare 16 fps; the Un-0 runtime declares 8 fps. GIF stores centisecond delays. Bound accumulated clip-duration quantization error by half of one centisecond; preserve frame pixels and order when correcting timing.",
    "Retain existing encoded-byte oracle results. A justified GIF timing correction requires a separate frame-pixel comparison plus the independent duration requirement; it cannot silently claim unchanged encoded bytes.",
    "Keep failed, unavailable and incomplete checks visible. Incomplete historical evidence supplies cases and hypotheses, not acceptance of new optimized execution.",
    "Krea numerical owner: internal/latentimage TestDenoiserResidentG2Distribution and TestFlowScheduleReproducesG2Exactly. Preserve the pinned fixture tolerances and report intermediate-only coverage. TestResidentLifetimeResourceAcceptance covers generation and cancellation, not perceptual equivalence.",
    "SimpleDiffusion numerical owner: internal/diffusionimage TestTinyModelForwardMatchesTorch; real artifact owner: TestRealCheckpointPublishesReferencePNG with modeltest. Preserve the native seed 7, two-step, 64x64 request separately from the retained 256x256 review cases.",
    "SenseNova owners: internal/sensenovarecipe TestSenseNovaGenerationLeadership and TestSenseNovaFullGenerationLeadership use the pinned smoke and full-generation manifests respectively. Preserve their scalar, grid and visual criteria; do not replace the full request with a shorter smoke request.",
    "Un-0 owners: internal/oscillatorimage TestArtifactPublishesReferencePNG, TestArtifactPublishesReferenceGIF, and TestArtifactGenerateDeterministicAndClassSensitive. Retain native artifact hash checks and explicit provenance limitations. Independent frame seeds do not establish temporal conditioning.",
    "Wan owners: internal/latentvideo TestDenoiserCUDASessionGoldenG3, TestDenoiserCUDASessionBF16G3, TestDenoiserCUDASessionGoldenG4, TestVAEDecodeCUDAGoldenG3 and TestVAEDecodeCUDAGoldenG4 with integration. Preserve existing sample-derived error criteria, dtype and sampling schedule. Tiny golden requests and the full clip are separate required cases.",
    "LiveEdit owners: internal/latentvideo TestLiveEditReferenceParity and TestLiveEditDeviceRuntime, plus internal/mediacapability TestVideoEditClipActivation. The retained tiny source-conditioned cases lack a full-quality native oracle; report that limitation rather than invent a quality threshold.",
    "Boundary and invalid-input checks use internal/latentvideo TestWanRequestFormAdmitsPromptOrTensors, TestReferenceEditRequestFormAdmitsClipOrTensors and TestVAEDecodeRejectsInvalidInputs. Preserve distinct prompt and tensor forms, explicit noise, declared geometry and source-artifact requirements. A seed change need not change output when the request supplies initial noise.",
    "Run device and model checks through the existing device-lane ownership with their required build tags. A skipped, absent or zero-match owner check remains unavailable and cannot satisfy the associated numerical requirement."
  ],
  "version": 1
}
